  "goodToKnow": "Der Justizminister (die Justizministerin) is the minister of justice, responsible for drafting laws in civil and criminal law, while courts themselves are independent. Germany has a federal Bundesjustizminister and one in each Land, where prisons and state prosecutors are run. Die Justiz is the justice system: die Justiz ist unabhängig. German J is pronounced like English y: yus-TEETS. Plural: die Justizminister."
